  "reason": "The strongest completed result is RNA-only multiprofile PCA with avgpool (config_002), clearly better than singleprofile PCA and transformer aggregation, while image-only ResNet is weak. The main remaining uncertainty is whether a learned RNA encoder can improve on PCA under the same favorable multiprofile/avgpool setting. config_005 changes only the RNA encoder from PCA to scvi_n200, keeping profile setting and aggregation fixed, so it directly isolates the representation effect. This is the best next experiment because it exploits the best-known profile/aggregation choice, tests a high-impact design decision, and avoids confounding by adding fusion or changing aggregation simultaneously."
